Z||000012||AkursedX||06-19-2001||01:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>Sweet, very nice GT!<P>I like the hardtop roof with the fastback.  Although most people prefer sunroofs, I'm not crazy about them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I seem to get that alot.  I like that hardtop too, but since I don't have a sunroof, I would like to have one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But hopefully soon, I plan on painting my roof black (ala:  1FST2M6)  I love how it gives the illusion of the targa top!  <P>I still have some engine and interior pics that I will post later on today after I figure out how to shrink them.<P>And thanks for the nice comments everyone!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slammed Fiero||06-19-2001||01:12 PM||||Sweeeeeet...<P>So whats done to it?? Looks a little lower , 5spd or auto???<P>Give us the Lowww Down<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000014||AkursedX||06-19-2001||01:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Sweeeeeet...<P>So whats done to it?? Looks a little lower , 5spd or auto???<P>Give us the Lowww Down<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok well here it goes:<P>Basic info:  88GT, automatic (yeah I know, I wish it was a 5 speed too), 93k miles, power mirrors, doors, and windows, performance subwoofer, beechwood interior, 2nd owner, no winters.<P>Engine:  Not rebuilt yet, stainless steel valves (done by previous owner), accel coil and ignition module, splitfire 8mm wires, Delco rapid fire plugs.  There hasn't been much done to the engine yet.  My engine project is this winter.  I plan on doing a high performance turbocharged 2.8.  I know I could go a number of other ways (It'll be around an 8k budget, but this is what I want to do, or maybe a v-8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Suspension:  KYB gr-2 struts in the rear, and the white KYB heavy duty shocks in the front.  Polyurethane all around, including swaybar endlinks.  The Fierostore sport spring kit, lowered 1 inch in the front, 7/8" in the rear.  <P>Tires and wheels were mentioned above  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Stereo:  Kenwood 4" component speakers in the front in homemade plates.  Blaupunkt overdrive 4x6's in the rear. Pioneer Premier 10inch sub, in one of Stimpy's custom footwell subboxes.  Boss 400 watt amp.  And a Panasonic reciever.  I can't remember the numbers, but it's got a sweet LCD, and 60x4 amp.  It's 450 bucks in crutchfield. I got it for 305  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And I think that's about all the mods I have in it.  But plenty more to come in the future  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Slammed Fiero, you should try to make it to Hamilton for the beach cruise on Monday nights.  I'm there every week, and I'd like to see your suspension setup.  I'll probably be at the Toronto show this year too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jake2m4||06-19-2001||01:43 PM||||Hey, that's one of the best looking fiero's I've seen.  I like the look of a gt minus the spoiler.  nice<P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||1
Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||06-19-2001||02:09 PM||||Should have my brakes done by the end of next week ..11.25" venteds all around.<P>I haven't driven my car all summer.<P>Washed it <BR>waxed it<BR>White face gauges done<BR>Fixed 2 relay's<BR>painted my mirrors<BR>cleaned a few little things<P>need to fix heater core (shi**y)<BR>get new rubber put on rear (255/40/17's are bald) have the tires.<P>Had some muffler hangers made..I hate when exhaust tips move all over ..looks dorky.<P>I'm hoping to have it all done and put together within the next 2 weeks if all goes well. <P>I also have a NOS kit in the works , I hope to send the Chq out tomorrow for it , if I get time. Then I get a whole slew of new projects. I have a set of 3.1ltr injectors , but I may change to a set of 350 IROC injectors , need a holley ADjustable Fuel pressure regulator. Ihave a line on some iroc injectors right now for $50 Canadian!!<P>We did a compression check on the motor over the weekend , it's perfect! I thought it may be stressed due to all the autocrosses and track events. I had it all checked out in prep for the NOS , I wanted no problems. But at 40,000 miles (22,000 are mine , 18,000 by an 86 yr old man) everything is perfect with the exception of a bad valve seal that leaks a bit of oil. I also got my hands on a remote oil filter kit. And to think some dumbasses thought my motor was Toast!! Silly kids.<P><BR>I got the NOS to tide me over until next summer when I swap out the 2.8. <P>So hopefully we can all get together this summer...a Fiero weekend at cayuga would be nice.. I'm hoping with the NOS setup I can net a high 13 sec pass.. off the bottle mid 15's.<P>I still have a bored out TB sitting on my desk.. so many projects..so little time. I had it bored to the coolant jackets , then had the coolant jackets filled with aluminum , then bored a bit more...I need to get the butterfly made for it , then on she goes!<BR> that should be worth around 4-6hp @ the wheels<P>We swapped the MSD 6A on our corvair V8 out for a 6AL , so now I have a 6A for my car FOR FREE!!! ..helps to ensure I get all the spark I need with NOS<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Ken Wittlief||06-19-2001||02:19 PM||||"a Fiero weekend at cayuga "<P>on second thought, maybe not<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||AkursedX||06-19-2001||03:03 PM||||Here's the rest of them.<P>Engine bay.  Note the color of my plenum, I guess it's a darker red than other intakes.  It must of been painted before I got it.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6180015_1.JPG">  <P>Interior shot.  It's Stimpy's footwell subbox in the footwell.  Plus I got plenty of stuffed animal mods!  Good for 40hp!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6180020_1.JPG">  <P>Another interior shot<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6180021.JPG">  <P>My amplifier located behind the passenger seat.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6180022.JPG">  <P>EDIT:  bad spelling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||14
